From 5288e53653e6abbfeee241de1e67f55b5c89dd6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Niccol=C3=B2=20Belli?= <niccolo.belli@linuxsystems.it>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:26:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Linux 7.3 compat: META
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bump Linux-Maximum to 7.3.

Upstream has not done this yet (master is still at 7.2), so this only
documents what the compat patches in this package already provide.  It
matters for two consumers of META: zfs-dkms-check would otherwise warn
that 7.3 is unsupported on every install, and ZFS_META_KVER_MAX ends up
in zfs_config.h.  DKMS builds themselves are unaffected either way,
since the PKGBUILD passes --enable-linux-experimental.

Signed-off-by: Niccolò Belli <niccolo.belli@linuxsystems.it>
---
 META | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/META b/META
index 8133bf1e3..2ae2e5777 100644
--- a/META
+++ b/META
@@ -6,5 +6,5 @@ Release:       1
 Release-Tags:  relext
 License:       CDDL
 Author:        OpenZFS
-Linux-Maximum: 7.2
+Linux-Maximum: 7.3
 Linux-Minimum: 4.18
-- 
2.55.0

